# EF Core 10 Breaking Changes for Your Code

## 1. `SetProperty` Generic Signature Change

In EF Core 10, `SetProperty` gained an additional type parameter for the **entity type**. The method is now `SetProperty<TEntity, TProperty>(...)` instead of `SetProperty<TProperty>(...)`.

**Fix** — add the entity type to `typeArguments`:

```csharp
setters = Expression.Lambda<Func<SetPropertyCalls<Blog>, SetPropertyCalls<Blog>>>(
    Expression.Call(
        instance: setters.Body,
        methodName: nameof(SetPropertyCalls<Blog>.SetProperty),
        typeArguments: new[] { typeof(Blog), typeof(string) },  // was: { typeof(string) }
        arguments: new Expression[]
        {
            Expression.Lambda<Func<Blog, string>>(
                Expression.Property(blogParameter, nameof(Blog.Name)), blogParameter),
            Expression.Constant("foo")
        }),
    setters.Parameters);
```

## 2. Complex Types — Column Name Disambiguation

EF Core 10 changed the default column naming for complex properties. Properties with the **same name** across different complex types (e.g., `ShippingAddress.Street` and `BillingAddress.Street`) now use a different disambiguation scheme. Existing migrations/databases will mismatch.

**Fix** — explicitly configure column names to match your existing schema:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b => {
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, a => {
        a.Property(x => x.Street).HasColumnName("ShippingAddress_Street");
    });
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, a => {
        a.Property(x => x.Street).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_Street");
    });
});

// For nested: explicitly name the full path
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>(b => {
    b.ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment, pay => {
        pay.ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress, addr => {
            addr.Property(x => x.City).HasColumnName("Payment_BillingAddress_City");
        });
    });
});
```

Or generate a new migration and apply the column renames to your database.

## 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — New `CommandSource` Parameter

EF Core 10 added a `CommandSource` parameter to the diagnostics methods.

**Fix:**

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        CommandSource commandSource)   // new required parameter
    { /* logging */ }
}
```

---

**Summary of changes:**

| Area | What broke | Fix |
|------|-----------|-----|
| `SetProperty` expression trees | Extra generic type param | Add entity type: `{ typeof(Blog), typeof(string) }` |
| Complex types | Column naming convention | Explicit `HasColumnName()` or new migration |
| Diagnostics logger | New `CommandSource` param | Add parameter to method signature |
